# Saved-page asset bundles from browser "Save As" — the .html is the fixture, the
# 8.6MB of images and vendor JS beside it is not.
tests/fixtures/*_files/

# Raw education payload captures are personal data (which courses this account
# has completed, when the current one ends). Only the scrubbed fixture that
# scripts/scrub-fixture.mjs emits is committed.
tests/fixtures/raw/

# Saved page captures embed a live session: userID, logoutHash, and a signed
# websocket JWT. Keep them local; the JSON payload is the fixture we test on.
tests/fixtures/*.html

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages.
.superpowers/

# Excel lock files, created while a workbook is open
~$*

# Tool artifact directory — visualizations are duplicated into docs/designs/
.codex/

# The nine community guides this project was specced from. Third-party forum
# content, kept locally for reference and removed from history before the repo
# went public (see docs/designs/v0.2.0-scope.md).
docs/initial-spec.md

# The beginner's-guide forum post and its working papers. Editorial content
# authored for Torn's forums, not part of the userscript — kept local so the
# published version lives on the forum rather than in two places. The route
# figures it quotes are still tested, via scripts/forum-post-data.js; only the
# prose draft is untracked. Verify a local draft with `npm run verify:forum`.
docs/forum-post.md
docs/designs/forum-post-plan.md
docs/Torn-Education-Beginner-Guide-proofing.docx
